# Royal Knight

## Lore

Royal knights are not the arrogant armchair warriors of the Knights of Nobility club. Many are kings, princes, lords and the children of the wealthy who hold to freedom and the code of chivalry as fiercely as any knight. What sets them apart is opportunity: they find tutors more easily, are better equipped and better educated (75% can read at least one language), and are schooled in the ways of court, so most dance well, may sing or play an instrument, and carry themselves with more polish than the average traveller.

## GM Notes

Weapons beyond the sheet: a sidearm and an energy rifle of choice. As with any knight, some favour magic or ancient weapons (usually high-tech versions such as vibro-blades, neuro-maces and tech-arrows), some purely modern arms and implants, most a mix. Some are partial or full conversion borgs.

Armor: as any knight, an M.D.C. environmental hard suit in the style of medieval plate, 60 to 100 M.D.C., fair to poor mobility, -10% to -20% to prowl, 17 to 25 pounds (7.7 to 11.3 kg), often with a detachable jet pack. Power armor may be used instead.

Mount: most ride a bionic or robot horse; some a hovercycle, motorcycle or A.T.V. with a jet pack; 20% ride an exotic animal such as a pegasus, unicorn, dragondactyl or gryphon (-10% to Horsemanship on these).

Money: 20,000 credits plus 3D6x100 credits'' worth of gems, precious metals or artifacts. Many are heirs to a fortune and may have limited access to family funds.

Cybernetics: the player may select two cybernetic (not bionic) implants at first level; any more must be bought.
', 'published', 'data-script'
